# ThermoWatch console -> FastAPI backend.
#
# Two modes (resolved once in src/services/api/client.ts - HTTP and WS always agree):
#
# SAME-ORIGIN (recommended for dev): leave VITE_API_URL UNSET. The Vite dev
#   proxy forwards /api, /v2 and /health to http://127.0.0.1:8000 (override the
#   target with TW_API_PROXY). No CORS round-trip, so a blocked preflight or
#   dead cross-origin hop can no longer surface as "Failed to fetch".
#
# DIRECT mode: uncomment VITE_API_URL below (or set it to a deployed backend).
#   Used by docker-compose and production (Vercel -> Render). Requires the
#   backend CORS allow-list to cover this site (TW_CORS_ORIGINS + TW_ORIGIN_REGEX),
#   and when THIS page is https the API origin must be https too (http -> mixed
#   content also shows as "Failed to fetch"). Vercel rewrites cover HTTP in
#   same-origin mode but NOT WebSocket upgrades - set VITE_API_URL in production
#   if the /v2/stream live feed must work there.
#
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
